# GitHub Learning Assistant (V1)

## Overview

GitHub Learning Assistant is a desktop application developed using Python Tkinter that helps students understand GitHub repositories before contributing to open-source projects.

The application retrieves repository information using the GitHub REST API, identifies technologies used in the project, generates beginner-friendly learning roadmaps, and stores analysis history using SQLite.

---

## Problem Statement

Many students discover interesting open-source repositories on GitHub but struggle to understand:

* What the project does
* Which technologies are used
* Whether the project is beginner-friendly
* What skills are required before contributing

This project simplifies repository exploration and learning.

---

## Objectives

* Learn GitHub API Integration
* Develop a GUI using Tkinter
* Store data using SQLite
* Practice GitHub collaboration workflows
* Generate learning recommendations

---

## Features

### Repository Analysis

* Repository Name
* Owner
* Description
* Primary Language
* Stars Count
* Forks Count
* Last Updated Date

### Learning Roadmap Generator

Generates technology-specific learning paths.

### Difficulty Prediction

Predicts repository difficulty using repository popularity metrics.

### Topics Detection

Displays repository topics and technologies.

### Contribution Suggestions

Provides beginner-friendly contribution recommendations.

### Analysis History

Stores and manages previous analyses using SQLite.

